<title>HUNGARY: Polish, Czech shares push CESI higher.</title>
<headline>Polish, Czech shares push CESI higher.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index advanced on Monday to end at 1,530.23 points, up 13.75 points or 0.91 percent, the Budapest Stock Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The index advanced due mainly to the gains of Polish and Czech shares.</p>
<p>The index, which has been published since February 1, reflects trends of 50 shares on the Budapest, Prague and Warsaw bourses.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
